WEBVTT

00:02.030 --> 00:04.360
Good morning, Manicia.

00:04.360 --> 00:06.140
Brother, good...

00:07.200 --> 00:10.610
Good morning. I'll bring out breakfast.

00:10.610 --> 00:12.550
Then, I'll help you.

00:12.550 --> 00:14.070
I can manage it myself.

00:17.550 --> 00:19.750
Master! Ms. Manicia!

00:19.750 --> 00:21.950
I'm sorry I was late preparing breakfast—

00:23.390 --> 00:24.420
You did it already?

00:25.870 --> 00:28.130
I see you're still not a morning person.

00:28.540 --> 00:30.330
Your bedhead is out of control.

00:32.260 --> 00:35.050
I'm embarrassed that I can't 
seem to do anything right.

00:35.590 --> 00:40.480
Don't worry about it. 
We help each other out.

00:40.480 --> 00:41.270
But...

00:41.620 --> 00:44.730
I feel like I'm not doing anything to help.

00:44.730 --> 00:46.490
That's not true.

00:46.490 --> 00:47.940
But it is.

00:48.460 --> 00:52.160
Not only have you allowed me
 to live a normal life,

00:52.160 --> 00:54.940
but you've taught me so much as well.

00:56.430 --> 01:00.370
Come to think of it, 
you two are rather knowledgeable.

01:00.370 --> 01:03.350
Who taught you what you know?

01:05.440 --> 01:06.790
I see.

01:07.000 --> 01:09.130
An apprenticeship, huh?

01:09.130 --> 01:11.250
Remember how I told you
we lived in the slums?

01:11.950 --> 01:16.720
The apprenticeship system is 
basically a master-student relationship.

01:17.360 --> 01:23.180
At the time, there was an effort by the nobles
 to return kids in the slums to a proper life.

01:23.760 --> 01:27.650
Because of that, 
we were able to attend knight school.

01:27.900 --> 01:29.610
Knight school?

01:32.560 --> 01:35.640
He can't do what he wants 
because of his sister.

01:35.640 --> 01:37.780
I feel sorry for Rud.

01:38.110 --> 01:39.130
Manicia.

01:39.850 --> 01:40.740
Manicia.

01:41.540 --> 01:42.310
Yes?

01:43.170 --> 01:46.080
I'm heading into town later. 
Is there anything you need?

01:46.080 --> 01:48.470
N-No, not particularly.

01:48.470 --> 01:49.530
Okay.

02:03.060 --> 02:12.900
<b>The Strongest Tank's Labyrinth Raids</b>

02:03.060 --> 02:12.900
<b>Labyrinth Raids</b>

02:03.060 --> 02:12.900
m 124 277 l 134 267 140 274 144 272 150 275 163 260 177 271 472 271 488 261 502 275 507 270 510 274 518 267 528 277 516 288 526 298 517 306 510 299 506 304 500 299 489 312 473 302 178 302 163 313 150 300 146 303 140 299 134 306 125 297 134 287

02:03.060 --> 02:12.900
A Tank with a Rare 9,999 Resistance Skill 
Got Kicked from the Hero's Party

03:28.180 --> 03:29.750
You're amazing, Rud.

03:29.750 --> 03:31.170
I'm super impressed.

03:31.170 --> 03:32.900
You'll definitely become a knight.

03:33.350 --> 03:37.360
<i>My brother was an incredible student 
who always achieved top marks.</i>

03:37.970 --> 03:41.940
<i>So everyone expected him 
to become a knight.</i>

03:43.040 --> 03:43.850
<i>But...</i>

03:44.870 --> 03:46.070
Did you hear?

03:46.070 --> 03:50.960
Apparently, Rud's becoming an adventurer
 to cure his sister's disease.

03:50.960 --> 03:52.000
No way.

03:52.260 --> 03:54.380
But he's so talented.

03:54.790 --> 03:57.840
He can't do what he wants 
because of his sister.

03:57.840 --> 03:59.880
I feel sorry for Rud.

04:01.410 --> 04:06.850
<i>My existence closed off the many paths 
that stretched before my brother.</i>

04:14.000 --> 04:14.940
Come in.

04:15.720 --> 04:18.020
Are you feeling unwell?

04:19.000 --> 04:22.740
I'm fine. I was just thinking about the past.

04:25.990 --> 04:27.150
Luna?

04:27.150 --> 04:31.120
You looked sad, so I wanted to cheer you up.

04:32.320 --> 04:35.620
I'm sorry. I couldn't come up 
with a better way to do it.

04:38.640 --> 04:40.550
Luna, if you...

04:41.400 --> 04:47.510
If you knew someone was throwing away 
their life for you, what would you do?

04:48.290 --> 04:52.130
They'd be much happier 
following another path,

04:52.640 --> 04:56.770
but they gave all of that up
 in order to live for you,

04:57.340 --> 05:01.520
even though they could've been 
much happier living another way.

05:02.640 --> 05:06.060
How would you interact 
with someone like that?

05:07.760 --> 05:09.370
I'm not sure.

05:09.370 --> 05:13.450
I don't know that anyone 
would go that far for me.

05:13.930 --> 05:20.140
But perhaps doing that is 
what makes that person happiest.

05:21.540 --> 05:24.090
What makes him happiest...

05:24.420 --> 05:26.990
You're talking about the master, aren't you?

05:26.990 --> 05:28.550
N-No.

05:30.430 --> 05:33.970
Why don't you try talking to him about it?

05:34.590 --> 05:38.860
He rescued me, an illegal homunculus.

05:38.860 --> 05:42.440
Perhaps the way he thinks 
is different from others.

05:43.050 --> 05:49.120
But I don't know how to 
interact with my brother.

05:50.880 --> 05:53.270
I don't think it's right 
to rely on him too much,

05:54.460 --> 05:57.550
so I try to keep as much distance 
between us as possible.

05:59.050 --> 06:02.500
But I really just want be kind to him.

06:02.990 --> 06:05.740
My head's a mess and
 I don't know what to do.

06:08.610 --> 06:11.970
Why don't you tell him 
everything you're feeling?

06:12.510 --> 06:13.230
What?

06:13.680 --> 06:20.150
<b>Skill:</b>

06:13.680 --> 06:20.150
<b>"Marker"</b>

06:14.270 --> 06:16.320
M-My brother's coming home!

06:16.320 --> 06:19.300
Wh-What should I do? 
Wh-What should I say?

06:20.830 --> 06:25.110
Others can only guess 
what a person is thinking.

06:28.000 --> 06:30.340
So try talking to him.

06:31.050 --> 06:32.830
Hup.

06:33.620 --> 06:37.790
I'm back, you two. 
Check it out. I was given all—

06:36.780 --> 06:37.790
Dear brother.

06:38.870 --> 06:41.290
There's something I'd like to ask you.

06:45.370 --> 06:46.210
What is it?

06:51.200 --> 06:52.140
<i>I'm scared.</i>

06:53.090 --> 06:58.230
<i>Wh-What if he regrets saving me?</i>

07:10.210 --> 07:13.240
Dear brother, are you happy 
with your current life?

07:13.660 --> 07:14.720
Of course I am.

07:15.980 --> 07:18.210
<i>How can he say that?</i>

07:18.210 --> 07:22.230
<i>He would've been happier 
following another path.</i>

07:22.960 --> 07:24.670
Wh-Why...

07:25.890 --> 07:29.630
Why did you save me when I was abandoned?

07:30.090 --> 07:31.510
That's because...

07:32.430 --> 07:35.640
You once saved me.

07:35.640 --> 07:38.020
What? I saved you?

07:40.460 --> 07:45.250
When we were little, remember how 
the other kids often called me scary

07:45.250 --> 07:48.330
because I was bigger than them 
and my face looked unfriendly?

07:49.350 --> 07:50.820
It's Old Man Rud.

07:50.820 --> 07:52.780
So scary. Run!

07:54.230 --> 07:56.360
But I just wanted to play.

07:58.510 --> 07:59.860
Brother.

08:01.150 --> 08:05.650
But you never acted 
like you were afraid of me.

08:05.650 --> 08:08.630
It made me happy every time.

08:09.290 --> 08:13.600
It's not like I didn't have doubts 
when I decided to live with you,

08:15.020 --> 08:18.990
but I still think I made the right choice.

08:20.190 --> 08:26.230
I love the time I spend with you. 
I'm happiest when I'm with you.

08:31.200 --> 08:32.650
I'm sorry.

08:33.390 --> 08:37.620
I assumed I knew how you felt.

08:38.320 --> 08:41.500
I thought you might be
 unhappy because of me.

08:42.390 --> 08:47.540
And when I thought about that, I didn't 
know how to interact with you anymore.

08:47.810 --> 08:51.000
Oh, uh, I've never been any good at that stuff.

08:51.000 --> 08:51.940
I'm sorry.

08:53.740 --> 08:55.300
I know.

08:55.300 --> 08:58.260
I know you better than anyone else.

08:58.740 --> 09:02.980
So I should've gotten my act together.

09:03.680 --> 09:06.400
I wouldn't say that, Manicia.

09:09.530 --> 09:10.150
Brother.

09:11.480 --> 09:13.320
Luna, thank you.

09:13.320 --> 09:15.610
I-I didn't do anything.

09:16.430 --> 09:21.830
If not for you, I would've 
worried about this forever, so...

09:22.370 --> 09:23.860
Thank you.

09:26.580 --> 09:31.030
I-It's nearly time for lunch. 
I-I'll prepare something to eat.

09:31.800 --> 09:33.510
Should we help her cook?

09:33.820 --> 09:34.420
Yes.

09:34.920 --> 09:35.880
Brother.

09:39.140 --> 09:42.810
Who dares disturb this blissful moment?

09:45.340 --> 09:47.120
It's good to see you again, Rud.

09:47.120 --> 09:48.860
Nin? Why are you here?

09:48.860 --> 09:51.600
I came to see you, of course.

09:51.600 --> 09:52.980
I got some time off.

09:53.240 --> 09:55.420
I'm surprised Kyglas allowed that.

09:56.030 --> 09:57.840
It wasn't Kyglas.

09:57.840 --> 09:59.450
The church granted me time off.

09:59.790 --> 10:00.640
What?

10:00.640 --> 10:03.430
I'm not a member of 
the hero's party anymore.

10:03.430 --> 10:04.410
What?

10:04.760 --> 10:09.370
After you left, we kept 
failing to clear labyrinths.

10:10.010 --> 10:12.530
So the hero's party disbanded.

10:14.190 --> 10:15.210
What?!

10:20.580 --> 10:23.270
All of you, prepare for combat.

10:27.380 --> 10:30.850
Lilia, what the hell are you doing?
 Get your act together!

10:30.850 --> 10:32.060
I <i>do</i> have it together!

10:37.830 --> 10:40.860
Damn it. Why can't I deal enough damage?

10:40.860 --> 10:43.200
Why have we lost so much 
of our absorb shields?

10:43.880 --> 10:46.160
<i>What's different from before?</i>

10:47.570 --> 10:49.000
Mr. Kyglas!

10:49.460 --> 10:51.840
The air is beginning to warp over there.

10:51.840 --> 10:53.710
More monsters are coming.

10:57.400 --> 10:59.250
Life Burst.

11:01.280 --> 11:05.640
<i>Activating my skill causes me to lose
 1,000 points of my absorb shield?</i>

11:05.640 --> 11:08.750
<i>I had no idea using Life Burst cost so much.</i>

11:09.590 --> 11:12.850
<i>Since he left, my skills have gotten weaker,</i>

11:12.850 --> 11:15.770
<i>and my shield's been depleting 
faster than before.</i>

11:16.860 --> 11:17.990
<i>Could it be?</i>

11:21.500 --> 11:23.120
No. No!

11:23.700 --> 11:24.570
I...

11:26.240 --> 11:28.040
I'm not wrong!

11:29.240 --> 11:30.110
Yes!

11:31.830 --> 11:34.000
<i>If I can just hit it one more time...</i>

11:35.090 --> 11:37.360
U-Um, Mr. Kyglas...

11:37.360 --> 11:37.880
What?

11:38.480 --> 11:42.130
Perhaps this floor is too high level for us.

11:42.450 --> 11:44.850
Forgive me, but we're allowing
 monsters to respawn

11:44.850 --> 11:46.810
because we can't kill them fast enough.

11:46.810 --> 11:47.770
Silence.

11:48.340 --> 11:49.890
Nin, hurry up and heal us.

11:50.410 --> 11:51.960
What are you saying?

11:51.960 --> 11:53.640
We can't retreat!

11:55.530 --> 11:57.650
We can't fail anymore.

11:58.260 --> 12:00.830
Life Burst!

12:02.100 --> 12:03.860
Huh? It's not activating?

12:11.690 --> 12:14.000
He lost his entire shield.

12:14.000 --> 12:14.920
Kyglas!

12:15.330 --> 12:19.310
W-Without my shield, it hurts so much.

12:31.300 --> 12:32.430
No!

12:42.050 --> 12:44.700
N-No! I don't want to die!

12:44.700 --> 12:46.820
I can't die!

12:49.400 --> 12:50.910
We're getting out of here, Lily!

12:51.190 --> 12:52.040
Got it.

12:52.420 --> 12:53.930
Dungeon Walk.

13:04.380 --> 13:05.470
Damn it!

13:06.110 --> 13:08.070
Evasion tank, my ass.

13:08.070 --> 13:11.680
Because of you, 
my reputation's been tarnished.

13:12.040 --> 13:13.640
W-We're sorry.

13:13.640 --> 13:15.190
Forgive us.

13:15.690 --> 13:16.950
You're wrong.

13:18.660 --> 13:20.620
It's not their fault.

13:21.060 --> 13:25.940
Both this time and the time before, 
it was your fault for recklessly charging in.

13:25.940 --> 13:26.570
What?

13:27.240 --> 13:29.310
When did you quit training?

13:30.650 --> 13:33.820
You're scrawny and unhealthy 
from drinking all the time.

13:34.800 --> 13:38.720
You've been relying on 
your Life Burst up to now.

13:38.720 --> 13:41.420
Did you really think it'd be 
enough to clear labyrinths?

13:41.420 --> 13:43.860
W-Well, it worked, didn't it?

13:43.860 --> 13:45.470
Because Rud was around!

13:46.470 --> 13:50.760
Now that Rud's gone, you've finally realized 
how your skill works, haven't you?

13:50.760 --> 13:52.180
I can tell.

13:52.860 --> 13:58.230
Life Burst enhances your physical abilities at
the cost of a major chunk of your absorb shield.

13:59.120 --> 14:01.610
That time Rud lost his entire shield,

14:01.610 --> 14:04.690
you'd just unleashed the biggest 
Life Burst you'd ever cast.

14:05.410 --> 14:11.360
Rud's unknown skill must have allowed him 
to treat others' shields as his own.

14:11.360 --> 14:15.330
You were pushing the cost 
of your skill onto Rud.

14:15.670 --> 14:20.880
Rud's shield value was 9,999. 
No wonder it made you so strong.

14:21.140 --> 14:24.130
You're wrong! That was all me!

14:24.130 --> 14:29.350
Losing one tank shouldn't 
s-screw things up this much.

14:29.350 --> 14:30.640
I'm the hero—

14:32.520 --> 14:35.140
Whatever. I'm quitting your party either way.

14:35.810 --> 14:38.480
It must be so easy blaming others
 for your shortcomings.

14:38.480 --> 14:40.170
I'm leaving as well. I'm sorry.

14:40.170 --> 14:43.230
I'm sorry. I'm not strong enough, either.

14:43.230 --> 14:46.690
Damn it. I'll recover soon enough
 and <i>prove</i> it to you.

14:46.690 --> 14:49.370
I'm the strongest! I'm the hero!

14:50.690 --> 14:52.180
So yeah...

14:52.180 --> 14:54.770
That's how the party disbanded.

14:54.770 --> 14:56.370
That sounds rough.

14:56.650 --> 14:59.940
I finally learned what 
my own skills do recently.

14:59.940 --> 15:01.330
I'm sorry for what I did.

15:01.680 --> 15:06.180
It's fine. We're also responsible 
for not figuring it out.

15:06.680 --> 15:08.720
Rud, I'm sorry for everything.

15:08.720 --> 15:09.350
What?

15:10.080 --> 15:14.500
I didn't know you were tanking 
the damage our shields were taking.

15:14.500 --> 15:18.020
We let our guard down. I'm sorry.

15:18.280 --> 15:20.360
That goes for me, too.

15:20.360 --> 15:23.670
I should've identified 
my unknown skills sooner.

15:24.160 --> 15:25.860
I'm sorry, too.

15:26.160 --> 15:27.730
In that case...

15:27.860 --> 15:32.070
No more talk about that. 
No point dwelling on the past forever.

15:32.600 --> 15:36.030
<i>She's always quick to flip her mood.</i>

15:39.290 --> 15:41.180
You're Manicia and Luna, right?

15:41.180 --> 15:42.770
Yes, Ms. Nin.

15:42.770 --> 15:44.420
Nice to meet you.

15:44.940 --> 15:49.670
I'm planning on checking out the orchard and 
stuff for a while, so I'll be seeing you around.

15:49.670 --> 15:51.630
What? For a while?

15:51.970 --> 15:54.210
What's that? You saying you want me to leave?

15:54.210 --> 15:56.240
No, that's not what I meant.

15:56.240 --> 15:58.340
There isn't a proper inn around here.

15:58.340 --> 16:01.670
We have the adventurers who 
sometimes visit stay in an empty home.

16:01.670 --> 16:03.810
O-Oh, really? What am I going to do?

16:04.340 --> 16:07.580
In that case, why don't you stay with us?

16:07.580 --> 16:08.640
Can I?

16:08.640 --> 16:10.280
If you don't mind staying in my room.

16:10.280 --> 16:13.280
Uh, Manicia, I didn't mention this before,

16:13.280 --> 16:15.960
but Nin's the daughter of 
a duke, making her nobility.

16:15.960 --> 16:16.630
What?

16:16.630 --> 16:17.900
She's a saint.

16:17.900 --> 16:18.490
What?

16:18.490 --> 16:21.870
Hey, don't bring that up!

16:21.870 --> 16:23.210
It's totally fine, Manicia.

16:23.210 --> 16:28.670
<i>I wouldn't want the church to rub us out for
providing inadequate facilities for a saint.</i>

16:29.820 --> 16:32.610
Anyway, you can sleep in my room.

16:32.610 --> 16:34.630
Wow, how spartan.

16:35.440 --> 16:38.990
But I suppose it suits you.
 It puts me at ease.

16:38.990 --> 16:41.560
I'll sleep in the living room.

16:41.840 --> 16:45.270
I don't mind sharing a room with you.

16:45.560 --> 16:47.340
Drop the act.

16:47.340 --> 16:49.230
What? You could tell?

16:49.830 --> 16:51.440
But, well...

16:51.670 --> 16:55.030
That wasn't a joke, you know.

16:57.510 --> 16:59.490
Rud! Are you there, Rud?

17:01.600 --> 17:02.540
Fille?

17:02.540 --> 17:03.520
Rud!

17:03.960 --> 17:04.790
The orchard...

17:06.240 --> 17:08.790
A monster I've never seen 
before has shown up there.

17:10.640 --> 17:11.800
The orchard...

17:12.340 --> 17:13.850
This is the work of a monster.

17:13.850 --> 17:15.280
We must defeat it quickly.

17:16.080 --> 17:19.110
I'm sorry you got dragged into this, Nin.

17:19.110 --> 17:23.050
Don't be so reserved. 
We used to be in the same party.

17:23.050 --> 17:24.230
Over there! That's it!

17:24.940 --> 17:26.940
A wolf? No, wait. A tiger?

17:27.530 --> 17:29.650
I can't see it clearly 
because of its magic essence.

17:29.650 --> 17:32.200
Magic essence? You mean that black miasma?

17:32.200 --> 17:34.360
Yeah. I'm gonna purge it.

17:39.530 --> 17:41.080
Nice work, Nin.

17:41.080 --> 17:42.770
Nothing I can't handle.

17:44.760 --> 17:51.380
<i>This monster's biological structure seems 
different from any I've encountered before.</i>

17:52.700 --> 17:56.050
<i>It's as if its magic essence 
has taken over its sense of self.</i>

18:02.460 --> 18:03.310
Are you okay?

18:04.320 --> 18:05.380
Rud.

18:05.380 --> 18:06.520
Mr. Vuild?

18:06.960 --> 18:08.550
Dad, are you okay?

18:08.550 --> 18:09.490
Sir.

18:09.920 --> 18:11.990
Sorry. I acted rashly.

18:12.830 --> 18:13.810
Watch out!

18:14.940 --> 18:16.160
<i>Provoke.</i>

18:18.000 --> 18:21.910
Those of you who can cast spells, 
keep chain-casting healing spells on me.

18:21.910 --> 18:23.480
Got it.

18:29.620 --> 18:30.330
Rud!

18:32.470 --> 18:34.800
Now's your chance to attack.

18:35.620 --> 18:39.840
I'll draw all the enemy's attacks!

18:48.400 --> 18:49.890
<i>They took a lot of damage.</i>

18:50.340 --> 18:51.710
Luna, here we go.

18:51.710 --> 18:52.480
Got it.

18:57.470 --> 18:59.280
Nice work, Nin and Luna.

18:59.280 --> 19:00.250
Master!

19:00.250 --> 19:03.780
We'll keep healing you. 
Go as hard as you want.

19:04.220 --> 19:06.100
Don't be scared. Get in there.

19:07.040 --> 19:12.710
My Shield of Sacrifice skill lets me tank
 the damage dealt to your absorb shields.

19:13.060 --> 19:16.060
That's the ultimate tanking skill.

19:16.060 --> 19:19.200
So you mean we can charge in 
without worrying about taking damage?

19:19.200 --> 19:19.800
Yeah.

19:20.150 --> 19:21.070
All right.

19:21.070 --> 19:22.430
Let's do this.

19:34.820 --> 19:35.720
It's fleeing.

19:36.620 --> 19:37.530
Don't let it escape!

19:37.530 --> 19:38.470
Crap.

19:38.470 --> 19:40.240
It's heading toward the town.

19:43.640 --> 19:45.240
A wall sprang up from the ground?

19:45.560 --> 19:46.440
Luna.

19:47.440 --> 19:48.580
All right.

19:52.390 --> 19:55.630
<i>I'll pour the 20,000 points 
of damage I've taken so far...</i>

19:55.950 --> 19:57.710
<i>into this one attack.</i>

19:59.220 --> 20:01.200
Life Conversion!

20:13.960 --> 20:16.270
<i>I overdid it!</i>

20:17.510 --> 20:21.730
<i>I think I caused more damage 
than the rampaging monster.</i>

20:21.730 --> 20:22.590
Rud.

20:23.550 --> 20:26.990
Thanks to you, we've defeated the 
monster without a single casualty.

20:27.260 --> 20:28.190
Thank you.

20:29.410 --> 20:30.810
<i>That's good.</i>

22:04.480 --> 22:07.930
So that was a C-rank black wolf?

22:08.390 --> 22:12.010
<i>But it was clearly as powerful
 as an A-rank monster.</i>

22:13.840 --> 22:15.220
Two magic stones?

22:15.480 --> 22:20.610
That's odd. All creatures capable 
of using magic have magic stones,

22:20.610 --> 22:22.320
but they normally only have one.

22:22.580 --> 22:27.640
Master, this magic stone resembles 
the ones used to create homunculi.

22:28.140 --> 22:33.340
Which means someone forced a 
homunculus's magic stone into a monster?

22:33.800 --> 22:35.540
Look at this.

22:35.540 --> 22:38.000
It looks like it was stitched together.

22:38.480 --> 22:43.440
In other words, 
someone created this monster.

22:43.440 --> 22:43.960
Yeah.

22:44.570 --> 22:48.780
Someone's using homunculus 
technology on monsters.

22:48.780 --> 22:54.180
But isn't creating homunculi 
for battle prohibited?

22:54.480 --> 22:58.120
It may be forbidden, but I'm sure 
there are many who are interested in it.

22:58.120 --> 22:59.390
You're right.

22:59.770 --> 23:04.360
Apparently, there are factories in the 
neighboring nation that employ only homunculi.

23:04.620 --> 23:10.320
<i>But if this was created for 
some purpose other than curiosity...</i>

23:11.340 --> 23:14.650
For now, we should report 
all of this to the local lord.

23:15.890 --> 23:22.590
<i>This attack by a monster with two magic stones 
was merely the harbinger of what was to come.</i>
